course: dictionary
lesson: 14010
title: Lyric: words of a song, and poems of feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may already know lyric from songs. The words of a song are its lyrics. «I can't remember the lyrics of the chorus.» Here lyrics means the words that are sung, not the tune.
explain: A lyric can also be a short poem. A lyric poem shows the poet's own feelings, often written as «I». «I miss the sea when the summer ends» tells the reader how the poet feels. Lyric poems are often written so they could be sung.
explain: Lyric can describe things too: «lyric poetry» is poetry that expresses strong personal feelings, like a song. When you meet a new word, look at the clues. Then swap in your meaning to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Lyric is a noun, and its plural is «lyrics».
fact: «Lyrics» means the words of a song.
fact: A lyric poem is a short poem about the poet's own feelings, often written in the first person, using «I».
fact: As an adjective, lyric means expressing strong personal feelings, like a song.
fact: Lyrics are covered by copyright, so you must not copy someone else's lyrics and claim them as your own.
exercise: Maya wrote the words for the class song. What are the words of a song called? | *Lyrics | Melodies | Pictures | Stanzas
exercise: «I wrote a lyric poem about missing my best friend.» What kind of poem is it? | *A short poem about the poet's own feelings | A list of facts about the weather | A long story about a dragon | A play with lots of actors
exercise: «Her lyric poetry made the whole room feel calm.» What does lyric mean in this sentence? | *Expressing strong personal feelings, like a song | Very large and grand | Describing a battle | Written in a foreign language
test: Ben copied the lyrics of his favourite band and said he wrote them himself. Why is this wrong? | *Lyrics are covered by copyright, so they belong to their writers | Lyrics are always too short to copy | Nothing, it is fine to do it | It is only wrong in maths lessons
test: Which sentence sounds most like a lyric poem? | *«I miss the sea and my grandad's laugh.» | «Plants need sunlight to grow.» | «Add two eggs and stir well.» | «The train left Leeds at nine o'clock.»
exam: Which sentence uses lyric as an adjective, describing a noun? | «The lyric was sung by the choir.» | «He read a lyric and then went to bed.» | «Sam learned three lyrics for the play.» | *«Her lyric poems made the whole class feel sad.»
